  "notes": "Modified cash basis audit. Governmental lines from the Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances - Governmental Funds (p5, Total Governmental Funds column); business-type lines from the proprietary funds statement (p7, Total Proprietary Funds column, includes depreciation; measure net position, as FY2023/FY2024). Business-type receipts total = operating 407,064 + nonoperating interest 197 (no single printed total); disbursements 383,978 as printed on the Statement of Activities (p2). Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position - Modified Cash Basis (p1), kept because it includes business-type capital assets, debt and interfund balances (governmental funds totals differ). No prior-year column, so beginning cash null; ending cash = governmental funds Cash and cash equivalents 48,191 (county treasurer 648 separate), investments 82,267. 'Other operating revenues' categorized charges for services because the Statement of Activities charges for services column (407,064) includes them. Keno Fund 'Other general receipts' 5,647 is keno/lottery by fund name (user ruling 2026-11-12); the statement-level 'Other general receipts' 8,432 stays one Total-column line. Capital outlay 11,400 (General Fund) is printed as General government - Capital improvements on the budget schedule (p9). Detail: the only supplementary schedule is the combined all-funds Budgetary Comparison Schedule - Primary Government (pp8-9), so detail is per fund column of the governmental funds (p5) and proprietary funds (p7) statements, as in FY2023; the budget schedule is not recorded. All roll-forwards tie. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
